For finding a value in an array, following code is available. Does the program execute and generate correct output? If not why? Modify the code.

```java
public class FindValue {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int [] array = [32, 87, 3, 589, 12, 1076, 2000, 8, 622, 127];
        int searchVal = 12;
        int i =0;
        boolean found = false;
        for(; i<array.length; i++)
        {
            if (array[i] == searchVal)
            {
                found = true;
            }
        }
        if (found)
        {
            System.out.println("Found " + searchVal + " at index "+ i);
        }
        else
        {
            System.out.println(searchVal + " not in the array ");
        }
    }
}
```

