Below is an attempt to make bubble sort a generic method so that it can sort all kinds of arrays,. Explain what happens when the following method is compiled?

```java
public class CounterDemo
{ <T> void bubbleSort(T[] data)
{ for(int a=1; a < data.length; a++)
for(int b=data.length-1; b >= a; b--)
{ if(data[b-1] > data[b])
{ // if out of order // exchange elements
T x = data[b-1];
data[b-1] = data[b];
data[b] = x;
}
}
}
}
